; saving and loading a game: the file is <name>.DAT in the game's folder,
; the name at F27EE:249C, made by make_path with no directory and
; extension 5. save_game takes the digit key pressed at its box (scancode
; 2..0Ah less 1, 0Bh 0) and T26EA:000F (a long, far text, width 2, flags
; 4: decimal digits, filled with '0' to the width) writes it as two
; digits: key 0 gives "00", key 3 "03" (a run: 03.DAT, 37815 bytes). save_game ran at D (a run, 00.DAT created and written),
; load_game at the start of a map when F27EE:250C bit 200h is set, after
; DISK, LOAD, a position and a key at "PLEASE INSERT DISK" (T1090:0867
; opens the file first to see that it is there).
